\ The complete five-part Pastafarian date relative to a calculation day.
\ Every choice is made from the canonical sauce and seal prescribed in
\ the main source of rules. The calculation day remains fixed, even
\ if the requested date lies in a much earlier or later year.
\
\ The output fields are:
\   year number since Creation,
\   canonical cutlet NAME index (not cutlet ordinal),
\   one-based day within its cutlet,
\   canonical month NAME index (not month ordinal),
\   one-based occurrence of that month through the requested day.
\
\ The current calendar-day axis still uses signed 32-bit numbers.
\ The memoized month weaving may be computationally prohibitive for
\ large realistic year/month combinations. This full-date entrypoint
\ is source only and HAS NOT BEEN TESTED WITH A CAL COMPILER.

\ CAL treats "within" as a preposition, so field names avoid that word.
A complete date answer has
  a number called year number,
  a number called cutlet name index,
  a number called cutlet day,
  a number called month name index,
  a number called month day.

The complete date answer is a complete date answer.
The complete date status is a number.
The complete date error is a string.

\ The five public numeric fields must be zero unless status is one.
\ Clear all fields before doing any work, not only after success.
To reset the complete date answer:
  Put 0 into the complete date status.
  Put 0 into the complete date answer's year number.
  Put 0 into the complete date answer's cutlet name index.
  Put 0 into the complete date answer's cutlet day.
  Put 0 into the complete date answer's month name index.
  Put 0 into the complete date answer's month day.
  Put "The complete calendar date was not resolved." into the complete date error.

\ Every required selection must succeed before any result is published.
To calculate complete date values given a calendar day and another calendar day:
  Reset the complete date answer.
  Check native day coordinate inputs given the calendar day and the other calendar day.
  If the native date input validity is no,
    put "The requested day is outside the currently safe 32-bit CAL range." into the complete date error; exit.
  Find the year for the calendar day and the other calendar day.
  If the year selection success is not 1,
    put "The requested Pastafarian year could not be selected within available resources." into the complete date error; exit.
  Find the restricted internal cutlet boundary.
  If the gate step budget's exhausted is 1,
    put "The exact gate search exceeded the bounded calculation budget." into the complete date error; exit.
  Choose the structural counts.
  Choose the canonical cutlet partition.
  If the cutlet partition's valid selection is not 1,
    put "The cutlet partition could not be selected." into the complete date error; exit.
  Verify the selected cutlet partition.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 1,
    put "The chosen cutlet partition has an invalid span count or total." into the complete date error; exit.
  Resolve the cutlet of the target day.
  If the gate step budget's exhausted is 1,
    put "The cutlet gate traversal exceeded the bounded calculation budget." into the complete date error; exit.
  If the requested cutlet number is 0,
    put "The requested day was not found inside the cutlet partition." into the complete date error; exit.
  Choose the canonical cutlet names.
  If the cutlet name choice's selection success is not 1,
    put "The cutlet name sequence could not be selected." into the complete date error; exit.
  Verify the selected cutlet names.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 1,
    put "The cutlet names have an invalid size or index." into the complete date error; exit.
  Read the requested cutlet name.
  If the requested cutlet name index is 0,
    put "The required cutlet name was not found." into the complete date error; exit.
  Choose the canonical month lengths.
  If the month length work's valid selection is not 1,
    put "The month length sequence could not be selected." into the complete date error; exit.
  Verify the selected month lengths.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 1,
    put "The month lengths do not form an exact permitted year." into the complete date error; exit.
  Choose the canonical month names.
  If the month name choice's selection success is not 1,
    put "The month name sequence could not be selected." into the complete date error; exit.
  Verify the selected month names.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 1,
    put "The month names have an invalid size or index." into the complete date error; exit.
  Put the target year day into the weaving selection's target position.
  Subtract the chosen year's opening day from the weaving selection's target position.
  Choose the canonical month weaving.
  If the weaving selection's resource limit reached is 1,
    put "The exact month weaving exceeded the safe memoization limit; no date was returned." into the complete date error; exit.
  If the weaving selection's selection success is not 1,
    put "The month weaving could not be selected." into the complete date error; exit.
  If the woven requested month ordinal is 0,
    put "The requested day was not found inside the woven months." into the complete date error; exit.
  Put the woven requested month ordinal into the requested month ordinal.
  Read the requested month name.
  If the requested month name index is 0,
    put "The woven month has no selected canonical name." into the complete date error; exit.
  Put the current year number into the complete date answer's year number.
  Put the requested cutlet name index into the complete date answer's cutlet name index.
  Put the requested cutlet day into the complete date answer's cutlet day.
  Put the requested month name index into the complete date answer's month name index.
  Put the woven requested month day into the complete date answer's month day.
  Put 1 into the complete date status.
  Put "" into the complete date error.

\ This wrapper tests the complete date at the canonical Foundation day.
\ It is a slow reference check and deliberately NOT part of To run.
To check the canonical complete Foundation date:
  Calculate complete date values given -15055671 and -15055671.
  If the complete date status is not 1,
    put "The complete Foundation date calculation did not succeed." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's year number is not 5000,
    put "Foundation has the wrong year number." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's cutlet name index is not 10,
    put "Foundation has the wrong cutlet name index." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's cutlet day is not 503,
    put "Foundation has the wrong day within its cutlet." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's month name index is not 20,
    put "Foundation has the wrong month name index." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's month day is not 56,
    put "Foundation has the wrong woven day within the month." into the check report; exit.
